{title: 299 - Forgive Our Sins as We Forgive}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #299 • DETROIT • C.M.}
{lyricist: Rosamond E. Herklots}
{composer: The Sacred Harp}
{key: Dm}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 299}
{meta: tune DETROIT}
{meta: meter C.M.}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]"Forgive [Gm]our [Am]sins [F]as we [C7]forgive,"
[Dm]You [F]taught [Gm]us, [Am]Lord, to [Dm]pray;
[A]But [Dm]You [C7]alone [Gm]can [F]grant us grace
[Am]To live [Gm]the words we [C]say.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]How [F]can [Gm]Your [Am]pardon [F]reach [C7]and bless
[Dm]The [F]unforgiving [Dm]heart
[A]That [Dm]broods [C7]on [A]wrongs [Gm]and [F]will not let
[Am]Old bitterness [Gm/D]depart?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm]In [F]blazing [Am]light [F]Your cross [C7]reveals
[Dm]The [F]truth [Gm]we [Am]dimly [Dm]knew:
[A]How [Dm]trifling [A]others' [F]debts to us;
[Am]How great [Gm]our debt to [C]You!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Dm]Lord, [F]cleanse [Gm]the [Am]depths [F]within [C7]our souls
[Dm]And [F]bid [Gm]resentment [Dm]cease;
[A]Then, [Dm]by [C7]Your [A]mercy [F]reconciled,
[Am]Our lives [Gm]will spread Your [C]peace.
{end_of_verse}
